d-count checks remain; future fingerprints require explicit verification. T11, 2026-10-10: explicitly pins 9e0fc92293b7 after exact agreement on all 44 historical neural cells, default and fixed options, bounded and running (test and validation delta=0, n_scored=205). The neural scorer adds optional per-document summed losses from the same logits; the default aggregate loss reduction, contexts, training, and model selection are unchanged. The F1c KenLM driver and scorer source are unchanged; native KenLM regression fits were not run under the one-thread limit. Existing strict settings/scored-count policy and all old pins remain; this source is not enrolled for inferred legacy counts. R4, 2026-10-11: explicitly pins 159507459e74 to the reviewed families of 9e0fc92293b7 after the existing integration regressions produced byte-equal scores on all 22 KenLM and 44 neural cells (default and fixed options, bounded and running). Stage 5 materializes optional document partitions and owned-artifact iterables before repeated use; default list inputs, contexts, fitting, validation/test loss arithmetic, settings and scored counts are unchanged. Iterator resource accounting no longer loses owned files after the first check. All historical pins and strict settings/scored-count checks remain; no missing count is inferred and no future fingerprint is authorized. R5, 2026-10-11: explicitly pins c755e98dea83 after exact independent comparisons on 22 KenLM cells against ee10afeebb21c95787fc7e5ff2ef29ebb3e190e0 and 44 neural cells against 5be16d1deded1eb8fae3f8a6f6b4861df21f67ca, all eleven rungs, both line treatments, default/fixed neural options. The neural comparison now loads the pinned historical scorer as well as historical corpora; earlier tests had incorrectly used the current neural scorer on both sides. An injected +1-bit current test loss is rejected in all 44 cells; the old comparison accepted it. Public Stage 5/6 boundaries now retain finite iterable declarations as recursive tuples; arrays, model/corpus objects, file handles and output sinks keep their native interfaces. Existing contexts, score arithmetic, fitting settings and scored counts are unchanged. The shared iterable helper is included in this fingerprint and runner/refit code identities. All old pins and strict scored-count/settings checks remain; no future source is authorized and no missing count is inferred. P7, 2026-10-13: explicitly pins c4c98f67369b to the reviewed families of c755e98dea83. The only change in the fingerprinted sources is the five-line retained-source header the freeze lock needs (a comment, two private imports and the __freeze_module_code__ and __freeze_source__ assignments) in src/stage5/rungs.py, nnlm.py, disk_space.py and iterables.py. The existing integration regressions produced byte-equal scores on all 22 KenLM cells against ee10afeebb21c95787fc7e5ff2ef29ebb3e190e0 and all 44 neural cells against 5be16d1deded1eb8fae3f8a6f6b4861df21f67ca (default and fixed options, bounded and running), and the injected +1-bit loss was rejected in all 44. All old pins and strict scored-count/settings checks remain; no future source is authorized and no missing count is inferred.",
